                        "sense_id": "8d296c0f-37ee-3d78-93e0-4b1ecb80aeef",
                        "entry_id": "28393b70-6f13-36e8-b77e-12a2d50288fb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not having been emptied."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "90694888-b886-4027-a6d5-38de310d8b93",
                                "sense_id": "8d296c0f-37ee-3d78-93e0-4b1ecb80aeef",
                                "text": "And thus each man hung, till the morning shin’d;‭\nWhich come, he knew the hour, and let abroad\n‭ His male-flocks first, the females unmilk’d stood\n‭ Bleating and braying, their full bags so sore\n‭ With being unemptied, but their shepherd more\n‭ With being unsighted; which was cause his mind\n‭ Went not a milking."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6055ddbb-42fd-4680-96f9-16be4a41e695",
                                "sense_id": "8d296c0f-37ee-3d78-93e0-4b1ecb80aeef",
                                "text": "[…] mounts in spray the skies, and thence again\nReturns in an unceasing shower, which round,\nWith its unemptied cloud of gentle rain,\nIs an eternal April to the ground,\nMaking it all one emerald."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "248a6d6a-5a5d-4752-a0ec-b39d185d8053",
                                "sense_id": "8d296c0f-37ee-3d78-93e0-4b1ecb80aeef",
                                "text": "Because the tide had been right to go, bedding had been stripped from the springs, food left about, water left unemptied to rust the kettles."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
